Insights: α↔polynomial P(x) (support 0..8). Condition ⇔ ∃Q(x) (Laurent) with P·Q=1+x^d ⇒ after removing smallest exponent a, P₁(x) must divide 1+x^d. Hence P₁ is product of distinct cyclotomic Φ_{2m} with all m sharing the same v₂. List Φ_{2m} of degree ≤8:  

v₂=0: m={1(1),3(2),5(4),7(6),9(6),15(8)}  
v₂=1: m={2(2),6(4),10(8)}  
v₂=2: m={4(4),12(8)}  
v₂=3: m={8(8)}  

For each v₂‑class, count subsets whose degree sum d≤8. Each subset gives P₁ (unique), sign ± (2 choices), and shift a∈[0,8−d] (9−d choices). Sum 2·(9−d) over all valid subsets (including empty set). This yields total shifty functions.
